e":320.36,"line":122},{"w":"God","s":320.36,"e":320.84,"line":122},{"w":"Screens","s":320.84,"e":321.18,"line":123},{"w":"may","s":321.18,"e":321.4,"line":123},{"w":"scan,","s":321.4,"e":321.76,"line":123},{"w":"but","s":321.76,"e":321.92,"line":123},{"w":"souls","s":321.92,"e":322.12,"line":123},{"w":"stay","s":322.12,"e":322.36,"line":123},{"w":"broad","s":322.36,"e":322.76,"line":123},{"w":"Storms","s":322.76,"e":323.2,"line":124},{"w":"may","s":323.2,"e":323.32,"line":124},{"w":"stalk","s":323.32,"e":323.6,"line":124},{"w":"and","s":323.6,"e":323.86,"line":124},{"w":"systems","s":323.86,"e":324.12,"line":124},{"w":"see","s":324.12,"e":324.48,"line":124},{"w":"But","s":324.48,"e":324.76,"line":125},{"w":"no","s":324.76,"e":325.02,"line":125},{"w":"machine","s":325.02,"e":325.38,"line":125},{"w":"can","s":325.38,"e":325.76,"line":125},{"w":"master","s":325.76,"e":326.44,"line":125},{"w":"me","s":326.44,"e":327.1,"line":125}],"lines":[{"s":5.38,"e":12.98,"text":"Yuh, baby believe this, yuh"},{"s":12.98,"e":16.28,"text":"Saints on the bus with the windows cracked"},{"s":17.8,"e":20.1,"text":"Storm in the sky, but the wheels stayed black"},{"s":20.1,"e":24.26,"text":"Qur’an, Gita, Bible, and *The Art of War*"},{"s":25.06,"e":28.26,"text":"All in my bag like I’d been here before"},{"s":28.26,"e":33.02,"text":"Twenty-three, still hungry, still holy, still haunted"},{"s":33.02,"e":36.66,"text":"Halo half-lit where the hard streets taunted"},{"s":36.66,"e":39.32,"text":"Headed for the water where the worldlines roar"},{"s":39.78,"e":43.38,"text":"And the sky kept asking, “What’s the metaphor?”"},{"s":44.12,"e":47.1,"text":"At twenty-three, I walked where sirens prayed"},{"s":47.76,"e":50.96,"text":"The cracked concrete became a parted sea"},{"s":50.96,"e":54.46,"text":"My mother marked my forehead, unafraid"},{"s":54.46,"e":58.34,"text":"And whispered, “Child, let God decide the key”"},{"s":58.26,"e":61.26,"text":"The billboards blinked like prophets selling doom"},{"s":61.88,"e":65.26,"text":"The cameras bowed like vultures in the rain"},{"s":65.26,"e":69,"text":"A thousand ads knew names inside my room"},{"s":69.74,"e":73.48,"text":"And dressed their lies in algorithmic flame"},{"s":73.48,"e":76.3,"text":"The handshakes had hands hidden in hands"},{"s":76.9,"e":80.22,"text":"The choir had wires woven in the walls"},{"s":80.22,"e":83.96,"text":"The saints sang soft of promised lands"},{"s":84.46,"e":87.7,"text":"While drones drew halos over project halls"},{"s":87.7,"e":91.72,"text":"But I kept psalms in pockets, prayers in code"},{"s":92.48,"e":95.46,"text":"A sacred sentence stitched beneath my tongue"},{"s":95.46,"e":99.24,"text":"The crooked compass trembled on the road"},{"s":99.36,"e":103.04,"text":"Like time itself had heard what I had sung"},{"s":103.46,"e":106.8,"text":"Pastor said, “There’s thunder in your name”"},{"s":106.8,"e":110.56,"text":"Deacon said, “Don’t bargain with the flood”"},{"s":110.56,"e":114.28,"text":"Driver said, “This route is not the same”"},{"s":114.28,"e":118.42,"text":"Then lightning signed the dashboard with my blood"},{"s":119.03,"e":121.7,"text":"We rode through the Bermuda rain"},{"s":121.7,"e":125.42,"text":"On a gospel bus with a ghost-lit flame"},{"s":125.68,"e":129.7,"text":"Time bent low when the thunder came"},{"s":129.7,"e":133.28,"text":"And Jesus called me by my name"},{"s":133.4,"e":135.5,"text":"Baby believe this, yuh"},{"s":135.42,"e":136.88,"text":"Baby believe this, yuh"},{"s":136.8,"e":138.88,"text":"When the tooltips flash and the heavens roar"},{"s":138.88,"e":140.72,"text":"Ask your soul, “What’s the metaphor?”"},{"s":141.44,"e":143.01,"text":"Baby believe this, yuh"},{"s":143.12,"e":144.78,"text":"Baby believe this, yuh"},{"s":144.78,"e":146.04,"text":"Twenty-three with a prophecy sewn"},{"s":146.04,"e":148,"text":"Through the triangle where the bright gates shone"},{"s":148,"e":148.86,"text":"Post-Chorus / Choir"},{"s":148.94,"e":149.96,"text":"What’s the metaphor?"},{"s":150.38,"e":153.1,"text":"Mercy marching through a locked front door"},{"s":153.1,"e":154.4,"text":"What’s the metaphor?"},{"s":154.42,"e":156.86,"text":"Poor boy chosen for a holy war"},{"s":156.86,"e":158.04,"text":"What’s the metaphor?"},{"s":158.16,"e":160.62,"text":"Truth in the storm that the rich ignore"},{"s":160.62,"e":161.8,"text":"What’s the metaphor?"},{"s":161.86,"e":165.08,"text":"God was the driver the whole time, Lord"},{"s":165,"e":167,"text":"The Baptist bus had Catholics in the back"},{"s":167,"e":168.9,"text":"A Muslim kid with moonlight in his stare"},{"s":168.9,"e":170.86,"text":"A Hindu girl with saffron on her track"},{"s":170.86,"e":172.72,"text":"And one old monk who vanished into prayer"},{"s":172.72,"e":174.56,"text":"Some carried beads, and some carried bruises"},{"s":174.56,"e":176.46,"text":"Some carried secrets the city refused"},{"s":176.46,"e":178.36,"text":"Some saw angels in emergency lights"},{"s":178.36,"e":180.08,"text":"Some saw demons in satellite news"},{"s":180.08,"e":182.04,"text":"We passed three ships in a spiral of years"},{"s":182.02,"e":183.88,"text":"One sailed with soldiers, one sailed with mirrors"},{"s":183.88,"e":185.78,"text":"One had a billboard that whispered, “Obey”"},{"s":185.78,"e":187.7,"text":"Then sold us our nightmares at half-price pay"},{"s":187.7,"e":189.56,"text":"The ocean opened its obsidian eye"},{"s":189.56,"e":191.4,"text":"The moon made a mouth in the mouth of the sky"},{"s":191.4,"e":193.22,"text":"The clock coughed blood, then the minutes reversed"},{"s":193.22,"e":195.2,"text":"And every last wound sang a hymn in the hearse"},{"s":195.2,"e":197.02,"text":"A girl in the back began humming “Amen”"},{"s":197.02,"e":198.94,"text":"The windows went white, then went black, then again"},{"s":198.94,"e":200.76,"text":"The preacher stood tall with his hand on the rail"},{"s":200.7,"e":202.68,"text":"Like Moses had boarded with Jonah’s whale"},{"s":202.68,"e":204.48,"text":"Then I saw a city where the poor don’t bleed"},{"s":204.48,"e":206.32,"text":"Where no child begs and no landlord feeds"},{"s":206.32,"e":208.22,"text":"Where the last kneel first and the first learn shame"},{"s":208.22,"e":210.32,"text":"Where the real Jesus walks with no brand-name fame"},{"s":210.32,"e":212.1,"text":"He wasn’t gold, He wasn’t for sale"},{"s":212.06,"e":214.04,"text":"No billboard crown, no sponsored veil"},{"s":214.04,"e":215.84,"text":"Dust on His robe, fire in His eyes"},{"s":215.84,"e":220.38,"text":"He said, “They can watch, but they can’t own skies”"},{"s":220.38,"e":222.54,"text":"We rode through the Bermuda rain"},{"s":222.54,"e":226.76,"text":"On a gospel bus with a ghost-lit flame"},{"s":226.76,"e":230.46,"text":"Time bent low when the thunder came"},{"s":230.46,"e":234.74,"text":"And Jesus called me by my name"},{"s":234.84,"e":236.86,"text":"Baby believe this, yuh"},{"s":236.86,"e":238.32,"text":"Baby believe this, yuh"},{"s":238.24,"e":240.16,"text":"When the tooltips flash and the heavens roar"},{"s":240.16,"e":241.98,"text":"Ask your soul, “What’s the metaphor?”"},{"s":242.22,"e":244.46,"text":"Baby believe this, yuh"},{"s":244.38,"e":246.04,"text":"Baby believe this, yuh"},{"s":246.04,"e":247.24,"text":"Twenty-three with a prophecy sewn"},{"s":247.24,"e":249.24,"text":"Through the triangle where the bright gates shone"},{"s":249.96,"e":252.94,"text":"He showed me wars that wore a friendly face"},{"s":252.94,"e":256.74,"text":"He showed me kings who kissed the poor for show"},{"s":256.74,"e":260.56,"text":"He showed me every hidden hand in place"},{"s":260.56,"e":264.74,"text":"Then showed me how to let the hatred go"},{"s":264.74,"e":267.5,"text":"He said, “Prophecy is not your panic"},{"s":267.5,"e":269.36,"text":"Power is not your rage"},{"s":269.36,"e":271.24,"text":"Mercy is militant magic"},{"s":271.24,"e":273.16,"text":"Love is lightning on the page”"},{"s":273.16,"e":275.38,"text":"He said, “The watcher cannot make you weak"},{"s":275.3,"e":277.16,"text":"The liar cannot make you less"},{"s":277.12,"e":279.04,"text":"The cameras cannot steal the meek"},{"s":279,"e":280.9,"text":"The storm cannot unbless the blessed”"},{"s":280.86,"e":282.82,"text":"So I came back breathing with a scar-shaped psalm"},{"s":282.82,"e":284.7,"text":"A thunderbolt tucked in my open palm"},{"s":284.7,"e":286.52,"text":"The city still stared, but it stared too late"},{"s":286.52,"e":288.4,"text":"I had bread for the hungry and keys to the gate"},{"s":288.4,"e":290.28,"text":"I had hymns for the hurt and a house for the lost"},{"s":290.28,"e":292.16,"text":"I had names of the poor carved into the cross"},{"s":292.16,"e":294.02,"text":"I had fire, not fury; I had faith, not fame"},{"s":294.02,"e":296.02,"text":"And the real Jesus still called my name"},{"s":296.02,"e":297.14,"text":"What’s the metaphor?"},{"s":297.54,"e":299.8,"text":"Maybe the screen was never the Lord"},{"s":300.02,"e":301.08,"text":"What’s the metaphor?"},{"s":301.28,"e":303.56,"text":"Maybe the wound became the sword"},{"s":303.76,"e":304.82,"text":"What’s the metaphor?"},{"s":305.08,"e":307.08,"text":"Maybe the map was made from scars"},{"s":307.5,"e":308.56,"text":"What’s the metaphor?"},{"s":308.82,"e":311.08,"text":"Maybe the saints were steering stars"},{"s":311.08,"e":312.34,"text":"What’s the metaphor?"},{"s":312.56,"e":314.2,"text":"Maybe the poor inherit more"},{"s":314.72,"e":316.04,"text":"What’s the metaphor?"},{"s":316.3,"e":319.04,"text":"Maybe heaven hid inside the war"},{"s":319.04,"e":320.84,"text":"Hands in hands, but God in God"},{"s":320.84,"e":322.76,"text":"Screens may scan, but souls stay broad"},{"s":322.76,"e":324.48,"text":"Storms may stalk and systems see"},{"s":324.48,"e":327.1,"text":"But no machine can master me"}],"duration":327.88,"source":"whisper-aligned","generatedAt":"2026-08-06T19:43:40.428Z","stats":{"whisperWords":898,"polishedWords":895,"matched":828,"matchRate":0.925}}